  6012                                  ; eth_send — send Ethernet frame pre-built at net_tx_buf via RTL8139
  6013                                  ;   IN:  net_tx_len = frame length
  6014                                  ;   OUT: net_send_state: 1=sent, 2=no NIC / still busy
  6015                                  ;   Standard RTL8139 register map (QEMU uses this, NOT RTL8139C+ variant):
  6016                                  ;     TSD0-3  = 0x10,0x14,0x18,0x1C (TX Status Desc 0-3: bits 0-12 = size,
  6017                                  ;                                    bit 13 = TxHostOwns, bit 15 = TOK/TSR)
  6018                                  ;     TSAD0-3 = 0x20,0x24,0x28,0x2C (TX Start Addr Desc 0-3: TX buffer phys addr)
  6019                                  ;   Writing size to TSDx triggers TX DMA. QEMU's rtl8139_transmit_one() refuses
  6020                                  ;   to retransmit on a descriptor still marked TxHostOwns (0x2000) from a prior
  6021                                  ;   TX, so eth_send rotates through all 4 descriptors via tx_tail.
